  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dfe0be8b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Education vs. divorce rate:** there's a clear, monotonic gradient here — divorce rate drops steadily as education rises, from ~63% at `less_than_hs` down to ~30% at `graduate`. That's more than a 2x difference between the extremes, so education level looks like a genuinely informative feature rather than noise.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Religious attendance vs. divorce rate:** by contrast, this one barely moves — all four categories sit in a tight 45–47% band. Despite being an intuitive variable to include, religious attendance doesn't separate the classes much on its own in this dataset."
   ]
  },
