   "source": [
    "**Which model wins, and why:** Logistic Regression slightly edges out Random Forest on every metric (accuracy 0.756 vs 0.746, ROC AUC 0.839 vs 0.823). Neither model is dramatically better, which suggests the relationship between these features and divorce is fairly linear/additive — the extra flexibility Random Forest offers to capture non-linear interactions isn't translating into better generalization here, and may even be costing it slightly through overfitting on a dataset of this size. Given the comparable (slightly better) performance and the added benefit of interpretability (coefficients can be inspected directly), Logistic Regression is the more sensible model to save and deploy — which is why it's the one persisted with `joblib` below."
   ]
